IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 2, Definitions (ss 2B to 2M).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively. The time words of Part 2 (business day, calendar
-- month, calendar year, financial year, month, sitting day) are in
-- au-interpretation-time.l4. Definitions that only point at another Act ("has the same
-- meaning as in the Public Service Act 1999") are borrowed terms, asked as facts, and
-- are `inert` in the coverage table. Whether a person is a body politic or corporate,
-- whether a relationship is "as a couple", and similar findings are INPUTS.

§ `Part 2: Definitions`

§§ `Section 2B: places (Australia, Commonwealth, Territory)`

DECLARE `A place` IS ONE OF
    `a State`
    `an internal Territory`
    `Norfolk Island`
    `the Territory of Christmas Island`
    `the Territory of Cocos (Keeling) Islands`
    `another external Territory`
    `a place outside Australia and the external Territories`

-- src:71 | Australia means the Commonwealth of Australia and, when used in a geographical sense, includes Norfolk Island, the Territory of Christmas Island and the Territory of Cocos (Keeling) Islands, but does not include any other external Territory.
-- src:84 | Commonwealth means the Commonwealth of Australia and, when used in a geographical sense, includes Norfolk Island, the Territory of Christmas Island and the Territory of Cocos (Keeling) Islands, but does not include any other external Territory.
-- src:115 | internal Territory means the Australian Capital Territory, the Northern Territory or the Jervis Bay Territory.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B "Australia", "Commonwealth", "internal Territory" (src:71-115)
GIVEN place IS A `A place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is within Australia in a geographical sense` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
    WHEN `a State`                                         THEN TRUE
    WHEN `an internal Territory`                           THEN TRUE
    WHEN `Norfolk Island`                                  THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Territory of Christmas Island`               THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the Territory of Cocos (Keeling) Islands`        THEN TRUE
    WHEN `another external Territory`                      THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a place outside Australia and the external Territories` THEN FALSE

-- src:102 | external Territory means a Territory, other than an internal Territory, where an Act makes provision for the government of the Territory as a Territory.
-- src:106 | foreign country means any country (whether or not an independent sovereign state) outside Australia and the external Territories.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B "external Territory", "foreign country" (src:102-106)
GIVEN place IS A `A place`
      `an Act makes provision for the government of the place as a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is an external Territory` place `an Act makes provision for the government of the place as a Territory` MEANS
    `an Act makes provision for the government of the place as a Territory`
    AND (   place EQUALS `Norfolk Island`
         OR place EQUALS `the Territory of Christmas Island`
         OR place EQUALS `the Territory of Cocos (Keeling) Islands`
         OR place EQUALS `another external Territory`)

@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B "foreign country" (src:106)
GIVEN place IS A `A place`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a foreign country` place MEANS
    place EQUALS `a place outside Australia and the external Territories`

§§ `Section 2B: document, contravene, prescribed, Proclamation, Senior Counsel`

-- src:94 | document means any record of information, and includes:
-- src:95 | (a) anything on which there is writing; and
-- src:96 | (b) anything on which there are marks, figures, symbols or perforations having a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them; and
-- src:97 | (c) anything from which sounds, images or writings can be reproduced with or without the aid of anything else; and
-- src:98 | (d) a map, plan, drawing or photograph.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B "document" (src:94-98)
GIVEN `it is a record of information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there is writing on it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are marks, figures, symbols or perforations on it that have a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sounds, images or writings can be reproduced from it, with or without the aid of anything else` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a map, plan, drawing or photograph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a document` `it is a record of information` `there is writing on it` `there are marks, figures, symbols or perforations on it that have a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them` `sounds, images or writings can be reproduced from it, with or without the aid of anything else` `it is a map, plan, drawing or photograph` MEANS
        `it is a record of information`
     OR `there is writing on it`
     OR `there are marks, figures, symbols or perforations on it that have a meaning for persons qualified to interpret them`
     OR `sounds, images or writings can be reproduced from it, with or without the aid of anything else`
     OR `it is a map, plan, drawing or photograph`

-- src:90 | contravene includes fail to comply with.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B "contravene" (src:90)
GIVEN `the person breaches the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person fails to comply with the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person contravenes the provision` `the person breaches the provision` `the person fails to comply with the provision` MEANS
    `the person breaches the provision` OR `the person fails to comply with the provision`

-- src:133 | prescribed means prescribed by the Act or by regulations under the Act.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B "prescribed" (src:133)
GIVEN `prescribed by the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed by regulations under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is prescribed` `prescribed by the Act` `prescribed by regulations under the Act` MEANS
    `prescribed by the Act` OR `prescribed by regulations under the Act`

-- src:134 | Proclamation means a Proclamation by the Governor-General that is registered in the Federal Register of Legislation established under the Legislation Act 2003 as a legislative instrument or notifiable instrument.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B "Proclamation" (src:134)
GIVEN `it is a Proclamation by the Governor-General` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is registered in the Federal Register of Legislation as a legislative instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is registered in the Federal Register of Legislation as a notifiable instrument` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a Proclamation` `it is a Proclamation by the Governor-General` `it is registered in the Federal Register of Legislation as a legislative instrument` `it is registered in the Federal Register of Legislation as a notifiable instrument` MEANS
        `it is a Proclamation by the Governor-General`
    AND (   `it is registered in the Federal Register of Legislation as a legislative instrument`
         OR `it is registered in the Federal Register of Legislation as a notifiable instrument`)

-- src:140 | Senior Counsel includes:
-- src:141 | (a) if the Sovereign is a King—King’s Counsel; and
-- src:142 | (b) if the Sovereign is a Queen—Queen’s Counsel.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2B "Senior Counsel" (src:140-142)
GIVEN `the person is of the rank of Senior Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Sovereign is a King and the person is King's Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Sovereign is a Queen and the person is Queen's Counsel` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is Senior Counsel` `the person is of the rank of Senior Counsel` `the Sovereign is a King and the person is King's Counsel` `the Sovereign is a Queen and the person is Queen's Counsel` MEANS
        `the person is of the rank of Senior Counsel`
     OR `the Sovereign is a King and the person is King's Counsel`
     OR `the Sovereign is a Queen and the person is Queen's Counsel`

§§ `Section 2C: persons`

DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `an individual`
    `a body politic`
    `a body corporate`

-- src:156 | 2C References to persons
-- src:157 | (1) In any Act, expressions used to denote persons generally (such as “person”, “party”, “someone”, “anyone”, “no-one”, “one”, “another” and “whoever”), include a body politic or corporate as well as an individual.
-- src:158 | (2) Express references in an Act to companies, corporations or bodies corporate do not imply that expressions in that Act, of the kind mentioned in subsection (1), do not include companies, corporations or bodies corporate.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2C (src:156-158)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is included in an expression denoting persons generally` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an individual`    THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a body politic`   THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a body corporate` THEN TRUE

§§ `Sections 2CA to 2F: spouses and de facto partners`

-- src:159 | 2CA References to spouses
-- src:160 | (1) For the purposes of any Act, a person is the spouse of another person (whether of the same sex or a different sex) if the person is legally married to the other person.
-- src:161 | (2) Subsection (1) has effect in addition to any provision of an Act that affects the meaning of spouse in a provision of that Act.
-- src:162 | Example: Spouse is defined for the purposes of an Act to include a de facto partner and a former spouse. Because of this section, a reference in the Act to a person’s spouse covers any person who is legally married to the person, in addition to any person covered by the definition in the Act.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2CA (src:159-162)
GIVEN `the person is legally married to the other person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is the spouse of the other person` `the person is legally married to the other person` MEANS
    `the person is legally married to the other person`

-- src:188 | (6) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(b), 2 persons are related by family if:
-- src:189 | (a) one is the child (including an adopted child) of the other; or
-- src:190 | (b) one is another descendant of the other (even if the relationship between them is traced through an adoptive parent); or
-- src:191 | (c) they have a parent in common (who may be an adoptive parent of either or both of them).
-- src:192 | For this purpose, disregard whether an adoption is declared void or has ceased to have effect.
-- src:193 | (7) For the purposes of subsection (6), adopted means adopted under the law of any place (whether in or out of Australia) relating to the adoption of children.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2F(6) and (7) (src:188-193)
GIVEN `one is the child, including an adopted child, of the other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `one is another descendant of the other, even through an adoptive parent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they have a parent in common, who may be an adoptive parent of either or both` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`are related by family` `one is the child, including an adopted child, of the other` `one is another descendant of the other, even through an adoptive parent` `they have a parent in common, who may be an adoptive parent of either or both` MEANS
        `one is the child, including an adopted child, of the other`
     OR `one is another descendant of the other, even through an adoptive parent`
     OR `they have a parent in common, who may be an adoptive parent of either or both`

-- 2F(4): persons who are not living together on a genuine domestic basis ONLY because of a
-- temporary absence, or illness or infirmity of either or both, are taken to be living
-- together. 2F(2) and (3): whether they have a relationship "as a couple" is a finding on
-- all the circumstances, none of which is necessary; the finding is an input.
-- src:169 | 2F De facto relationships
-- src:170 | (1) For the purposes of paragraph 2D(b), a person is in a de facto relationship with another person if the persons:
-- src:171 | (a) are not legally married to each other; and
-- src:172 | (b) are not related by family (see subsection (6)); and
-- src:173 | (c) have a relationship as a couple living together on a genuine domestic basis.
-- src:174 | (2) In determining for the purposes of paragraph (1)(c) whether 2 persons have a relationship as a couple, all the circumstances of their relationship are to be taken into account, including any or all of the following circumstances:
-- src:175 | (a) the duration of the relationship;
-- src:176 | (b) the nature and extent of their common residence;
-- src:177 | (c) whether a sexual relationship exists;
-- src:178 | (d) the degree of financial dependence or interdependence, and any arrangements for financial support, between them;
-- src:179 | (e) the ownership, use and acquisition of their property;
-- src:180 | (f) the degree of mutual commitment to a shared life;
-- src:181 | (g) the care and support of children;
-- src:182 | (h) the reputation and public aspects of the relationship.
-- src:183 | (3) No particular finding in relation to any circumstance mentioned in subsection (2) is necessary in determining whether 2 persons have a relationship as a couple for the purposes of paragraph (1)(c).
-- src:184 | (4) For the purposes of paragraph (1)(c), the persons are taken to be living together on a genuine domestic basis if the persons are not living together on a genuine domestic basis only because of:
-- src:185 | (a) a temporary absence from each other; or
-- src:186 | (b) illness or infirmity of either or both of them.
-- src:187 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (1), a de facto relationship can exist even if one of the persons is legally married to someone else or is in a registered relationship (within the meaning of section 2E) with someone else or is in another de facto relationship.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2F(1) to (5) (src:169-187)
GIVEN `they are legally married to each other` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are related by family` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they have a relationship as a couple` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they live together on a genuine domestic basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they do not live together only because of a temporary absence, or illness or infirmity` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`are in a de facto relationship` `they are legally married to each other` `they are related by family` `they have a relationship as a couple` `they live together on a genuine domestic basis` `they do not live together only because of a temporary absence, or illness or infirmity` MEANS
        (NOT `they are legally married to each other`)
    AND (NOT `they are related by family`)
    AND `they have a relationship as a couple`
    AND (   `they live together on a genuine domestic basis`
         OR `they do not live together only because of a temporary absence, or illness or infirmity`)

-- src:167 | 2E Registered relationships
-- src:168 | For the purposes of paragraph 2D(a), a person is in a registered relationship with another person if the relationship between the persons is registered under a prescribed law of a State or Territory as a prescribed kind of relationship.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2E (src:167-168)
GIVEN `the relationship is registered under a prescribed law of a State or Territory as a prescribed kind of relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`are in a registered relationship` `the relationship is registered under a prescribed law of a State or Territory as a prescribed kind of relationship` MEANS
    `the relationship is registered under a prescribed law of a State or Territory as a prescribed kind of relationship`

-- src:163 | 2D References to de facto partners
-- src:164 | For the purposes of a provision of an Act that is a provision in which de facto partner has the meaning given by this Act, a person is the de facto partner of another person (whether of the same sex or a different sex) if:
-- src:165 | (a) the person is in a registered relationship with the other person under section 2E; or
-- src:166 | (b) the person is in a de facto relationship with the other person under section 2F.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2D (src:163-166)
GIVEN `they are in a registered relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `they are in a de facto relationship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`are de facto partners` `they are in a registered relationship` `they are in a de facto relationship` MEANS
    `they are in a registered relationship` OR `they are in a de facto relationship`

§§ `Sections 2H, 2J, 2K`

-- src:209 | 2H References to law of the Commonwealth
-- src:210 | In any Act, a reference to the law of the Commonwealth, or to a law of the Commonwealth, does not include, and is taken never to have included, a reference to a law in force in a Territory so far as the law is so in force because of an Act providing for the acceptance, administration or government of that Territory.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2H (src:209-210)
GIVEN `it is a law in force in a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in force in the Territory because of an Act providing for the acceptance, administration or government of the Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is a law of the Commonwealth, apart from the Territory exclusion` `it is a law in force in a Territory` `it is in force in the Territory because of an Act providing for the acceptance, administration or government of the Territory` MEANS
    NOT (`it is a law in force in a Territory` AND `it is in force in the Territory because of an Act providing for the acceptance, administration or government of the Territory`)

-- src:211 | 2J Documents commencing proceedings
-- src:212 | A reference in a provision of an Act to any one or more of the following in connection with court proceedings:
-- src:213 | (a) a summons;
-- src:214 | (b) an information;
-- src:215 | (c) a claim;
-- src:216 | (d) a complaint;
-- src:217 | (e) a declaration;
-- src:218 | is taken to include a reference to any document through which proceedings may be instituted in a court.
-- src:219 | Note: An example of such a document is a court attendance notice under the Criminal Procedure Act 1986 of New South Wales.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2J (src:211-219)
GIVEN `the reference is to a summons, an information, a claim, a complaint or a declaration, in connection with court proceedings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `proceedings may be instituted in a court through the document` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the reference is taken to include the document` `the reference is to a summons, an information, a claim, a complaint or a declaration, in connection with court proceedings` `proceedings may be instituted in a court through the document` MEANS
    `the reference is to a summons, an information, a claim, a complaint or a declaration, in connection with court proceedings`
    AND `proceedings may be instituted in a court through the document`

-- src:220 | 2K Rules of court
-- src:221 | (1) In any Act, rules of court, in relation to any court, means rules made by the authority having for the time being power to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of such court.
-- src:222 | (2) The power of the authority to make rules of court includes a power to make rules of court for the purpose of any Act which directs or authorises anything to be done by rules of court.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 2K (src:220-222)
GIVEN `made by the authority with power for the time being to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`are rules of court` `made by the authority with power for the time being to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court` MEANS
    `made by the authority with power for the time being to make rules or orders regulating the practice and procedure of the court`
